The scorer was calibrated in the wedding repo: after the clause
punctuation fix, its three densest real messages scored 5.5-8.6 and
plain rewrites of them 4.2 or less, while the caricatures in
SLOP_VARIANTS score 13.8-32. Step 5's bands are those numbers.

The obvious objection is Goodhart: the model writing the message can
read the metric it is graded by. But gaming it means shorter
sentences and fewer abstract nouns, which is what the skill wants
anyway. The stock-phrase list is the only place gaming and quality
diverge, and it contributes nothing on honest drafts.

textstat is imported unconditionally, so the skill picks up a hard
dependency the rest of the plugin lacks. It is installed globally
here; if that proves fragile the import could go lazy and step 5
become skippable with a warning.
